The Faust libraries (stdfaust.lib), bundled inside faustwasm
  https://github.com/grame-cncm/faustlibraries

  The modules in modules/ import these libraries. The page compiles each module
  in the browser, and the compiled module then contains the library functions
  it calls. Read from the library sources bundled in faustwasm 0.20.2:

  - fi.highpass, fi.lowpass, fi.tf1 and ve.moogLadder declare STK-4.3, an
    MIT-style licence.
  - The other functions the modules call declare no licence of their own and
    fall under the header of their library file: the LGPL, version 2.1 or
    later, with the Faust exception, which lets a larger work that contains
    the library carry any licence. These are an.amp_follower_ar, ba.countdown,
    ba.sAndH, ba.tau2pole, de.fdelay, en.adsr, en.ar, ma.PI, ma.SR, ma.frac,
    ma.tanh, no.noise, no.pink_noise, os.osc, os.oscp, os.sawtooth, os.square,
    re.zita_rev1_stereo, si.smoo and si.smooth.

  Some functions in these libraries declare GPL-3.0-only, among them the
  look-ahead limiters in compressors.lib. The modules here call none of them,
  and the Output module carries its own limiter for that reason. Before a new
  module calls a library function, look for its `declare <name> license` line
  in the library source.

